{# https://www.home-assistant.io/docs/configuration/templating/#reusing-templates #}

{#
Check whether a person is home, confirmed by more than one source.

Arriving needs two of HomeKit, GPS and WiFi to agree, or GPS home on its own for 5 min, so a
GPS jump near home doesn't count. Leaving needs both HomeKit and GPS away, so a WiFi drop
can't flip it (false departures re-trigger arrival automations).

Wifi only counts towards arriving: being on the home SSID means home, but being off it doesn't
mean away (WiFi off, low power mode, out of range in the garden, or a stale sensor).

:param homekit_entity: The input boolean set by the HomeKit arrive/leave automations.
:param person_entity: The person entity, home when GPS puts them in the home zone.
:param ssid_entity: The companion app's SSID sensor for their phone.
:param home_ssid: The home WiFi's SSID.
:param current_state: The presence sensor's own state (this.state), as rules differ for arriving and leaving.

:returns: True if present, else False.
#}
{%- macro check_presence(homekit_entity, person_entity, ssid_entity, home_ssid, current_state) -%}
  {%- set homekit = is_state(homekit_entity, 'on') -%}
  {%- set gps = is_state(person_entity, 'home') -%}
  {%- set wifi = is_state(ssid_entity, home_ssid) -%}
  {%- set gps_held = gps and now() - states[person_entity].last_changed >= timedelta(minutes=5) -%}
  {%- set votes = [homekit, gps, wifi] | select | list | count -%}
  {%- if current_state == 'on' -%}
    {{ homekit or gps }}
  {%- else -%}
    {{ votes >= 2 or gps_held }}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}
